<article class="env-definition" id="03OO">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03OO">Definition <span data-tag="03OO">59.18.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category. Given a presheaf of sets $\mathcal{G}$, we define the <em>free abelian presheaf on $\mathcal{G}$</em>, denoted $\mathbf{Z}_\mathcal {G}$, by the rule </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathbf{Z}_\mathcal {G}(U) = \mathbf{Z}[\mathcal{G}(U)]  \]
</div>
  <p> for $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$ with restriction maps induced by the restriction maps of $\mathcal{G}$. In the special case $\mathcal{G} = h_ U$ we write simply $\mathbf{Z}_ U = \mathbf{Z}_{h_ U}$. </p>
</article>